This is a fresh repo - https://github.com/itforankit/devin_repo.git . Bootstrap and build an Agentic RAG System end to end:
SETUP(do this first):
1.	Create requirements.txt with all dependencies (use a vector store that runs locally, e.g. Chroma or FAISS, plus OpenAI for embedding/LLM – my OPENAI_API_KEY is available as an environment variable).
2.	Create an AGENTS.md describing the project structure and conventions (tests required, no secret in code, lint before PRs).
3.	Create attesting skill at .agents/skills/test-app/ documenting exactly how to install, run and test this app – you’ll use it yourself before every PR.
BUILD:
4.	Ingestion: load PDF, DOCX and text file, chunk them, embed them, store in the vector store.
5.	Retrieval agent: an agent that decides when retrieval is needed, what to query, and answers with citations to source chunks.
6.	Eval harness: a script that runs a fixed question set and scores the agentic system against a naïve single-shot retrieval baseline, printing a comparison table.
7.	Web UI: a simple chat interface (streamlit + a smal frontend) where I can upload a document and ask question and track latency.
Rules:
-	Work in small commits; open a pr for each working slice.
-	Write tests for core logic and make them pass.
-	Before any PR that touches the UI, run the app and test it using the test-app skill, and attach a video recording of the test.
